CNN vs Vision Transformer (ViT) Image Classification

Overview
This project compares CNN (ResNet18) and Vision Transformer (ViT) for image classification using the CIFAR-10 dataset.

Technologies Used
- Python
- PyTorch
- Torchvision
- Hugging Face Transformers
- Matplotlib
- Pandas

Dataset
CIFAR-10 contains images from 10 classes: airplane, automobile, bird, cat, deer, dog, frog, horse, ship, and truck.

- Training images: 5,000
- Testing images: 2,000

Models Used
1. CNN (ResNet18)
- Uses a pre-trained ResNet18 model.
- Trains the final classification layer for 10 classes.

2. Vision Transformer (ViT)
- Uses a pre-trained Vision Transformer model.
- Trains the classification layer for 10 classes.

Methodology
1. Load and preprocess the CIFAR-10 dataset.
2. Resize and normalize images.
3. Load and configure both models.
4. Train both models for 2 epochs.
5. Evaluate accuracy and testing time.
6. Compare predictions using graphs and sample images.

Results
The models are compared based on classification accuracy, evaluation time, and prediction results. Bar charts are used to visualize the comparison.

Conclusion
This project compares CNN and Vision Transformer models for image classification and helps understand their performance differences in terms of accuracy and evaluation time.
